<article class="env-definition" id="0834">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0834">Definition <span data-tag="0834">67.17.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subspace. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The scheme theoretic image of the morphism $U \to X$ is called the <em>scheme theoretic closure of $U$ in $X$</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $U$ is <em>scheme theoretically dense in $X$</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0833" data-tag="0833">67.17.2</a> are satisfied. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>